# Proposed by the swarm (2026-10-14); the documenter may edit or drop it.
# Story: at the desk, on a display of 2560 points, Xcode, Safari and Slack are docked side by side and a Finder window floats. Typing in
# Xcode, the person presses the Show Everything shortcut. Xcode stays a window and keeps the keyboard: no docked window becomes a tile
# for the Desktop's sake, and what floats on a Desktop that is a tile shows over the arrangement.
# Reference: T03 T20, F61.
display-size 2560x1440 25
open Xcode 1400x900 min 960x600
open Safari 1324x940 min 574x240
open Slack 1100x750 min 760x500
dock 101 left
dock 102 right
dock 103 right
open Finder 920x436 min 501x252
focus 101
type
key ctrl+opt+space
expect visible 101
expect visible 102
expect visible 103
expect visible 104
expect focused 101
